@meeting crossingBackOath
// The ending (E-1, EN2 for lead 39; plans/ending-spec.html, "The crossing back"): Sunday Day 35, the bow lounge, after the
// horn at 14:30. You lead the first-timers' oath for Basil (the words the Captain read you on Day 7, now yours: the
// Line's crossingCeremony with you as host); Brennan's punch; Saruth reads the Veyli ship's last signal. The Captain's
// final address follows: crossingBackAddress.stay or .go by your answer to the offer (29a), or .ask (she asks you at
// the front, Stay or Go only) if you haven't answered or said "not sure". A stand-in for SW6's words. They/them for
// you; Saruth they/them; Basil he/him (design-doc).
title: Crossing back
from: Captain Odile Marrow
gist: The Wren crossed back over the Line. You led the oath for Basil, Saruth read the Veyli ship's last signal, and the Captain spoke to the crew.
== lines
marrow: Thank you all. Four weeks ago we crossed into the reach as guests. Today we cross back as friends of it.   [gesture]
marrow > you: This time the oath isn't mine to read. {me}, the front is yours.
you: First-timers, step forward. Don't be shy.
bramwell-basil: That's just me, isn't it? Right. Stepping.   [laugh]
you: "We have crossed the Line. We left the near stars behind us, and we did not go alone."
you: "Whatever is out here, we meet it as one crew, and we bring each other home."
you: "From today, this reach knows our names."
bramwell-basil: Do I say something now? I feel like I should say something.
? choice
* Say what you like. It's yours.   rel:bramwell-basil+1
  bramwell-basil: Then... thank you for having me. All of you. Even the punch.   [laugh]
* "We're glad we came." That's what I'd say.   rel:bramwell-basil+1
  bramwell-basil: We're glad we came. Yes. That.   [nod]
brennan: Line punch. One mug each, first-timer first. Drink it all. No faces.   [gesture]
bramwell-basil: It's green. Why is it still green?
brennan: Tradition. Drink.   [nod]
saruth: Captain. Taavek's ship sends its last signal. May I read it?   [gesture]
marrow: Please.
saruth: "Go well, Wren. The reach remembers the ones who were kind in it. Come back over the Line again, one day."
marrow: Thank you, Saruth. Tell them the Wren says the same.   [nod]
